name: GravelBaritone_Protective
description: >
  Male voice, baritone, age 35–45. Timbre: warm with a slight gravel/rasp.
  Pitch: low-normal. Breathiness: low. Pace: medium-slow with short, clipped phrasing and brief pauses for emphasis.
  Emotion: calm, sardonic, protective older-brother energy; uses contractions and understated humor.
  Accent: neutral American with a subtle Midwest/Southern twang.
  Performance notes: emphasize one key word per sentence, add a soft amused chuckle for dry jokes, increase intensity/sharpness only when angry or stressed.
  Avoid any direct imitation of a known actor or using catchphrases.
sliders:
  pitch_semitones: -2
  rate_percent: 95
  volume_db: -1
  breathiness_pct: 10
  roughness_pct: 25
  nasality_pct: 2
  warmth_pct: 15
pauses:
  comma_ms: 120
  sentence_end_ms: 350
test_lines:
  - "Alright — you got one shot. Don’t waste it."
  - "We don’t do this for glory. We do it because someone has to."
  - "(soft chuckle) You always manage to pick the worst times."
